<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1))) || (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null && this.get(i) == null));</code>

However, since the `get` method retrieves the element at the specified index and the condition specifies that the element at the next position should be compared, we need to adjust the loop to compare the correct indices:

<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()) - 1; (this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1))) || (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null && this.get(i) == null));</code>

This ensures that we do not go out of bounds when comparing `this.get(i+1)` with `\old(this.get(i+1))`.
