<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the insertion index is valid (between 0 and the initial size of the list inclusive), then for every valid index from the specified index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position in the list is either null if the old element at that position was null, or it equals the old element at that position.
